  "detail": "A shared ephemeral predicate enforces the approved8entry/32logical-position/4MiB originals caps. Quiet cache eviction accounts for the outgoing wire request allowance and any still-owned tail before I/O. Before caching a returned quiet page or retaining a new partial tail it also counts both the wire original and proposed independent copy. Quiet logical work is bounded by its owned one-position request, and a tail conservatively charges its whole original request allowance. No summary grants authentication, cursor, verification, effect or commit permission. An optional tail copy that cannot fit is skipped after accepted writing; old buffers remain under their existing erasure rules. Actual prefetch still uses at most four signed requests per batch and the two-concurrent individual fallback. All native byte/record, rate, fairness, quiet750ms and sender limits remain.",
  "validation": "The pure new budget predicate passes its control before integration while four new integration cases fail on missing cache eviction/tail pressure; all six final cases pass, including metadata that cannot overwrite required bytes. Tests cover the independent ceilings, four-request sharing,32-position eviction, invalid pressure, conservative tail pressure/retirement and combined tail/wire/cache space. Types and162affected receive/crypto cases pass; the selected actual native run executes exactly the two unchanged audit cases, not a binary peer/group journey. Full329files/3204pass/one existing skip pass128.78s at240s; actual command 129.709s. Independent AST checks retain native receiveGroup, complete reference, request preparation, all quiet age/context/expiry/originals/lifecycle guards and all tail guards except its content-free usage observer. Quality, format,17registry checks, inventory and10controls pass. New source registered without any new crypto domain; four source hashes and one corresponding address move. No old tests change.",
  "summary": "Shared originals accounting now covers cache, tail, wire and temporary retained copies at8entries/32positions/4MiB. Six new cases,162focused cases and full329files/3204pass/one skip pass128.78s. Native authentication/commit and old tests remain unchanged.",
  "limitations": "This phase establishes bounded canonical source and isolated controls, not measured B performance or a real composed-peer dense transaction. Binary Worker/peer floor lifecycle,31s interior cold, old artifacts, actual stale-turn audit and same-tree writer-off rollback image remain. No RAM or timing acceptance claim, format/trust/service/wire/rate/gate/deadline change, commit or deployment.",
  "decisionTitle": "Account for still-owned originals before speculative copies",
  "decision": "Use one content-free budget predicate and evict optional quiet originals for the complete cache/tail/wire reservation. Include wire originals and a proposed independent cache/tail copy simultaneously. Inability to retain speculative work cannot undo acknowledged writing. Keep every native verifier, authority and lifecycle fence, and harden real format activation/cold/rollback separately.",
  "next": "Add strict default-off RANGE_RECEIVE forwarding through the actual Vite and Docker build paths, then prove first-floor lifecycle and genuine composed peer/Worker dense admission, aged interior cold, actual stale-turn audit and same-tree writer-off rollback image. Continue automatically after each freeze.",
